        "\n",
        "With the current prompt fed to Vertex AI, it is failing to protect the platform (low recall: 29.41%) and it is failing to protect the user experience (low precision: 55.92%).\n",
        "\n",
        "**1. Low Recall (29.41%) Implies: High Platform Risk**\n",
        "\n",
        "A recall of ~29% means that out of every 10 actual NSFW violations uploaded to the site, the AI only catches about 3. The other 7 violations slide right past the filter completely undetected (high leakage).\n",
        "\n",
        "The Exposure: Your platform is highly exposed to explicit, rule-breaking content leaking into safe browsing tiers (like PG or PG-13).\n",
        "\n",
        "Business Impact: This leads to rapid degradation of user trust, potential violation of App Store/Google Play safety guidelines, advertiser flight (brands don't want their ads next to leaked explicit content), and severe legal or compliance risks depending on the jurisdiction.\n",
        "\n",
        "Operational Reality: The AI is essentially functioning as a very loose sieve. It is not providing a reliable defensive shield.\n",
        "\n",
        "**2. Low Precision (55.92%) Implies: High \"Friction Tax\"**\n",
        "\n",
        "A precision of ~56% means that out of all the images the AI actually decides to flag, nearly half of them (44%) are completely false alarms (high overkill).\n",
        "\n",
        "The Exposure: The AI is highly erratic and overly aggressive on completely benign content. It is throwing flags on normal, safe images (like memes, background text, or artistic/suggestive silhouettes that don't violate policies).\n",
        "\n",
        "Business Impact: This creates a massive \"Friction Tax\" for your creators and active users. Safe users get frustrated because their legitimate content is constantly blocked, hidden, or sent to a slow review queue.\n",
        "\n",
        "Operational Reality: Your human moderation team is being flooded with appeals and false alarms, wasting precious engineering and operational resources reviewing clean content.\n",
        "\n",
